(An `On error` that DRAINS whatever flag an earlier statement left
 standing, so the handler that follows the statement under test reports
 that statement and nothing else. The flag is consumed by the handler
 that catches it and is not sticky (hand-verified), so one drain is
 enough. Without this, a leaf that asserts "no error happened" would fire
 on a flag some unrelated leaf raised twenty lines earlier - a false
 finding that looks exactly like a real one.)

To 'gen drain the error flag' with a text called indent and a text called 'the witness name'.
    a text called 'the drain line' is "{indent}On error Set {'the witness name'} to 0.\n".
