     rather than cosmetic.)
    'gen emit' of "\n".
    (The local form, carrying the argument. A call's argument must be a
     name rather than a literal in the `append <call> to <list>` position
     this leaf's sibling uses, and a local reads better everywhere else,
     so the argument goes through one either way.)
    a text called 'the argument phrase' is 'gen fresh noun'.
    a text called 'the argument name' is 'gen written name' of 'the argument phrase'.
    a text called 'the argument declaration' is "{indent}a value called {'the argument name'} is {'the argument literal'}.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the argument declaration'.
    (The local form again, this time initialised from the call - which is
     what makes the return form observable at all.)
    a text called 'the result phrase' is 'gen fresh noun'.
    a text called 'the result name' is 'gen written name' of 'the result phrase'.
    a text called 'the result possessive' is 'gen possessive name' of 'the result phrase'.
    a text called 'the result declaration' is "{indent}a value called {'the result name'} is {'the function name'} of {'the argument name'}.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the result declaration'.
    a text called 'the predicate' is 'gen tag predicate' of 'the returned tag'.
    a text called 'the tag name' is 'gen tag name' of 'the returned tag'.
    a text called 'the tag it reported' is 'gen type phrase' of 'the result possessive'.
    a text called 'the tag assertion' is "{indent}If {'the result name'} is not {'the predicate'} then, Print \"ASSERT VAL-02: expected {'the tag name'} got {'the tag it reported'}\", Exit 95.\n".
