        a text called 'the shown literal' is 'gen value shown' of 'the returned tag' and 'the returned payload',
        a text called 'what came back' is 'gen got phrase' of 'the result name' and 'the result possessive' and 'the returned tag',
        a text called 'the payload assertion' is "{indent}If {'the result name'} is not {'the returned literal'} then, Print \"ASSERT VAL-02: expected {'the shown literal'} got {'what came back'}\", Exit 95.\n",
        'gen emit' of 'the payload assertion'.
    (The third shape of the local form: no initialiser. Emitted, never
     asserted - see this leaf's own note. Whether it appears at all is
     unpinned, so it is drawn.)
    a number called 'the bare local choice' is 'rng below' of 2.
    If 'the bare local choice' is 0 then,
        a text called 'the bare phrase' is 'gen fresh noun',
        a text called 'the bare name' is 'gen written name' of 'the bare phrase',
        a text called 'the bare possessive' is 'gen possessive name' of 'the bare phrase',
        a text called 'the bare declaration' is "{indent}a value called {'the bare name'}.\n",
        'gen emit' of 'the bare declaration',
        a text called 'the bare print' is "{indent}Print {'the bare possessive'} type.\n",
        'gen emit' of 'the bare print'.
    'gen emit' of "{indent}Print {'the result name'}.\n".

(VAL-04 (LANGUAGE.md:2677-2680): inside the callee a `value`
 parameter's `is a ...` predicates read its tag and printing dispatches
 on it, and the parameter can be forwarded or appended back into a list
 with the tag preserved.

 This is the POSITIVE half of the dispatch claim, and it is the half
 'gen leaf value dispatch' cannot make. That leaf asserts from inside
 the callee, which sees one argument at a time and cannot know which of
 several the caller is on, so it can only assert the negative - that a
 tag it never passed never fires. Here each branch names ITSELF, by
 returning a text the caller compares against the tag it passed: if the
 compiler ever routed an argument to the wrong branch, the two disagree
 and the row fires.

 Every branch returns the same declared type, which LANGUAGE.md:2811
 says is what makes a conditionally-returning function carry a return
 type at all - the mixed-type case is VAL-32's limitation and is not
 emitted here.

 The forward half appends the value returned by a `value` function
 straight into a list and reads the slot back into a `value` local,
 asserting the tag and (for a scalar) the payload survived the round
 trip through the list.)

To 'gen leaf value dispatch label' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    a text called 'the classifier phrase' is 'gen fresh verb'.
    a text called 'the classifier name' is 'gen written name' of 'the classifier phrase'.
    a text called 'the parameter phrase' is 'gen value parameter name'.
    a text called 'the parameter name' is 'gen written name' of 'the parameter phrase'.
    a number called 'the label style' is 'rng below' of 3.
    a text called 'the definition line' is "{indent}To {'the classifier name'} with a value called {'the parameter name'}.\n".
    'gen open a function definition'.
    'gen emit' of 'the definition line'.
    (Branch order is rotated because nothing pins it: the six predicates
     are mutually exclusive, so any order classifies the same.)
    a number called 'the rotation' is 'rng below' of 6.
    a number called offset is 0.
    While offset is less than 6,
        a number called 'the slot' is offset add 'the rotation',
        a number called 'the tag under test' is 'the slot' modulo 6,
        a text called 'the predicate' is 'gen tag predicate' of 'the tag under test',
        a text called 'the tag name' is 'gen tag name' of 'the tag under test',
        a text called 'the label' is 'gen branch label' of 'the label style' and 'the tag name',
        a text called opener is "Otherwise if",
        If offset is 0 then,
            Set opener to "If".
        a text called 'the branch line' is "{indent}    {opener} {'the parameter name'} is {'the predicate'}, Return a text, \"{'the label'}\".\n",
        'gen emit' of 'the branch line',
        Set offset to offset add 1.
    (`nothing` matches no predicate (LANGUAGE.md:2845), so it is what
     the closing branch is for and what the caller expects when it
     passes one.)
    a text called 'the absent label' is 'gen branch label' of 'the label style' and "nothing".
    a text called 'the closing branch' is "{indent}    Otherwise, Return a text, \"{'the absent label'}\".\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the closing branch'.
    (LANGUAGE.md:91 - a blank line after a function definition, required
     rather than cosmetic.)
    'gen emit' of "\n".
    a number called 'how many arguments' is 'rng below' of 4 add 1.
    a number called 'arguments made' is 0.
    While 'arguments made' is less than 'how many arguments',
        a number called 'the argument tag' is 'rng below' of 7,
        a text called 'the payload' is 'gen value payload' of 'the argument tag',
        a text called 'the literal' is 'gen value expression' of 'the argument tag' and 'the payload',
        a text called 'the argument tag name' is 'gen tag name' of 'the argument tag',
        a text called 'the expected label' is 'gen branch label' of 'the label style' and 'the argument tag name',
        a text called 'the argument phrase' is 'gen fresh noun',
        a text called 'the argument name' is 'gen written name' of 'the argument phrase',
        a text called 'the branch phrase' is 'gen fresh noun',
        a text called 'the branch name' is 'gen written name' of 'the branch phrase',
        a text called 'the argument declaration' is "{indent}a value called {'the argument name'} is {'the literal'}.\n",
        'gen emit' of 'the argument declaration',
        a text called 'the call line' is "{indent}a text called {'the branch name'} is {'the classifier name'} of {'the argument name'}.\n",
        'gen emit' of 'the call line',
        a text called 'the branch assertion' is "{indent}If {'the branch name'} is not \"{'the expected label'}\" then, Print \"ASSERT VAL-04: expected {'the expected label'} got {{{'the branch name'}}}\", Exit 95.\n",
        'gen emit' of 'the branch assertion',
        Set 'arguments made' to 'arguments made' add 1.
    'gen leaf value forwarding' of indent and 'the classifier name'.

(VAL-04's forward half, called by the leaf above: a `value` returned by
 a `value` function is appended into a list and read back out of the
 slot with its tag intact - the manual's own `append echo of item to
 out` shape, asserted rather than printed.

 The forwarding function is a SECOND definition because the classifier
 above returns a text, and it is the tag surviving a `value` return that
 this half is about.)

To 'gen leaf value forwarding' with a text called indent and a text called 'the classifier name'.
    a text called 'the forwarder phrase' is 'gen fresh verb'.
    a text called 'the forwarder name' is 'gen written name' of 'the forwarder phrase'.
    a text called 'the parameter phrase' is 'gen value parameter name'.
    a text called 'the parameter name' is 'gen written name' of 'the parameter phrase'.
    a text called 'the definition line' is "{indent}To {'the forwarder name'} with a value called {'the parameter name'}. Return a value, {'the parameter name'}.\n".
    'gen open a function definition'.
    'gen emit' of 'the definition line'.
    'gen emit' of "\n".
    a number called 'the tag' is 'rng below' of 6.
    a text called 'the payload' is 'gen value payload' of 'the tag'.
    a text called 'the literal' is 'gen value expression' of 'the tag' and 'the payload'.
    a text called 'the offering phrase' is 'gen fresh noun'.
    a text called 'the offering name' is 'gen written name' of 'the offering phrase'.
    a text called 'the tally phrase' is 'gen fresh noun'.
    a text called 'the tally name' is 'gen written name' of 'the tally phrase'.
    a text called 'the slot phrase' is 'gen fresh noun'.
    a text called 'the slot name' is 'gen written name' of 'the slot phrase'.
    a text called 'the slot possessive' is 'gen possessive name' of 'the slot phrase'.
    (How many slots the value lands in, and which one is read back. The
     manual's example appends to an empty list; nothing says the list
