    'gen emit' of "{indent}a value called {'the offering name'} is {'the literal'}.\n".
    'gen emit' of "{indent}a list called {'the tally name'} is [].\n".
    a number called 'forwards made' is 0.
    While 'forwards made' is less than 'how many forwards',
        a text called 'the append line' is "{indent}append {'the forwarder name'} of {'the offering name'} to {'the tally name'}.\n",
        'gen emit' of 'the append line',
        Set 'forwards made' to 'forwards made' add 1.
    'gen emit' of "{indent}a value called {'the slot name'} is element {'the slot read back'} of {'the tally name'}.\n".
    a text called 'the predicate' is 'gen tag predicate' of 'the tag'.
    a text called 'the tag name' is 'gen tag name' of 'the tag'.
    a text called 'the tag it reported' is 'gen type phrase' of 'the slot possessive'.
    a text called 'the tag assertion' is "{indent}If {'the slot name'} is not {'the predicate'} then, Print \"ASSERT VAL-04: expected {'the tag name'} out of the list got {'the tag it reported'}\", Exit 95.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the tag assertion'.
    If 'the tag' is less than 4 then,
        a text called 'the shown literal' is 'gen value shown' of 'the tag' and 'the payload',
        a text called 'what came back' is 'gen got phrase' of 'the slot name' and 'the slot possessive' and 'the tag',
        a text called 'the payload assertion' is "{indent}If {'the slot name'} is not {'the literal'} then, Print \"ASSERT VAL-04: expected {'the shown literal'} out of the list got {'what came back'}\", Exit 95.\n",
        'gen emit' of 'the payload assertion'.
    'gen emit' of "{indent}Print {'the tally name'}.\n".

(VAL-12 (LANGUAGE.md:2753-2755): after a successful in-place retype the
 variable is tracked with the NEW type for the rest of its lifetime, and
 retyping to the type it already holds is a no-op.

 Two claims, two halves, both in one leaf because the second is only
 meaningful beside the first.

 The tracking half is asserted three ways, because "tracked as the new
 type" has three observable consequences and a compiler could get any
 one of them right while losing the others: the new type's predicate
 answers true, the OLD type's predicate answers false, and - where the
 new type is a number - arithmetic on the variable works and gives the
 sum the generator computed. Arithmetic is the operation that is valid
 ONLY after the retype: on an untouched `value` it is a compile error
 (VAL-08, LANGUAGE.md:2711), so its succeeding here is the tracking
 working.

 The no-op half asserts the payload is unchanged, the tag is unchanged,
 and no error flag was raised - the last through a drained handler, so a
 flag left standing by an earlier leaf cannot masquerade as this one's.)

To 'gen leaf value retype tracking' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    (0 number, 1 text, 2 float, 3 boolean - the four retype targets
     LANGUAGE.md:2722 names. The source is written as the text spelling
     of the answer, which is the manual's own worked shape and the only
     one where the generator knows the converted result exactly.)
    a number called 'the target' is 'rng below' of 4.
    a text called 'the source payload' is 'gen retype source' of 'the target'.
    a text called 'the phrase' is 'gen fresh noun'.
    a text called 'the name' is 'gen written name' of 'the phrase'.
    a text called 'the possessive' is 'gen possessive name' of 'the phrase'.
    a text called 'the target predicate' is 'gen tag predicate' of 'the target'.
    a text called 'the target tag name' is 'gen tag name' of 'the target'.
    a text called 'the target type text' is 'gen dynamic type text' of 'the target'.
    a text called 'the tag it reported' is 'gen type phrase' of 'the possessive'.
    (A text target starts from a number so the conversion has something
     to do; the other three start from the text spelling of the answer,
     so the tag it starts under is a text.)
    a number called 'the source tag' is 1.
    a text called 'the source literal' is "\"{'the source payload'}\"".
    If 'the target' is 1 then,
        Set 'the source tag' to 0,
        Set 'the source literal' to 'the source payload'.
    a text called 'the source predicate' is 'gen tag predicate' of 'the source tag'.
    a text called 'the source bare tag name' is 'gen bare tag name' of 'the source tag'.
    'gen emit' of "{indent}a value called {'the name'} is {'the source literal'}.\n".
    'gen emit' of "{indent}{'the name'} is {'the target predicate'}.\n".
    a text called 'the new tag assertion' is "{indent}If {'the name'} is not {'the target predicate'} then, Print \"ASSERT VAL-12: expected {'the target tag name'} after the retype got {'the tag it reported'}\", Exit 95.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the new tag assertion'.
    a text called 'the old tag assertion' is "{indent}If {'the name'} is {'the source predicate'} then, Print \"ASSERT VAL-12: expected the {'the source bare tag name'} tag to be gone got {'the tag it reported'}\", Exit 95.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the old tag assertion'.
    a text called 'the type assertion' is "{indent}If {'the possessive'} type is not \"{'the target type text'}\" then, Print \"ASSERT VAL-12: expected {'the target type text'} got {'the tag it reported'}\", Exit 95.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the type assertion'.
    (The operation that is valid only for the new type. A number target
     is the one whose result the generator can compute, so it is the one
     that carries the arithmetic; the other three make the tracking
     claim through the two predicates above.)
    If 'the target' is 0 then,
        a number called 'the numeral' is 'the source payload' as a number,
        a number called addend is 'rng below' of 1000 add 1,
        a number called 'the sum' is 'the numeral' add addend,
        a text called 'the arithmetic assertion' is "{indent}If {'the name'} add {addend} is not {'the sum'} then, Print \"ASSERT VAL-12: expected {'the sum'} got {{{'the name'} add {addend}}}\", Exit 95.\n",
        'gen emit' of 'the arithmetic assertion'.
    (The no-op half: retype it again to the type it now holds.)
    a text called 'the witness phrase' is 'gen fresh noun'.
    a text called 'the witness name' is 'gen written name' of 'the witness phrase'.
    'gen emit' of "{indent}a number called {'the witness name'} is 0.\n".
    'gen drain the error flag' of indent and 'the witness name'.
    'gen emit' of "{indent}{'the name'} is {'the target predicate'}.\n".
    'gen emit' of "{indent}On error Set {'the witness name'} to 1.\n".
    a text called 'the quiet assertion' is "{indent}If {'the witness name'} is not 0 then, Print \"ASSERT VAL-12: expected no error retyping to {'the target tag name'} it already holds got {{{'the witness name'}}}\", Exit 95.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the quiet assertion'.
    a text called 'the unchanged tag assertion' is "{indent}If {'the possessive'} type is not \"{'the target type text'}\" then, Print \"ASSERT VAL-12: expected {'the target type text'} after the no-op got {'the tag it reported'}\", Exit 95.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the unchanged tag assertion'.
    (The payload after the no-op. A float's payload interpolates as its
     bit pattern rather than its digits (this file's own note), so the
     comparison is written for every target but the reported value is
     the tag where the payload cannot be shown.)
    a text called 'the comparison' is 'the source payload'.
    If 'the target' is 1 then,
        Set 'the comparison' to "\"{'the source payload'}\"".
    a text called 'what it holds' is 'gen got phrase' of 'the name' and 'the possessive' and 'the target'.
    a text called 'the payload assertion' is "{indent}If {'the name'} is not {'the comparison'} then, Print \"ASSERT VAL-12: expected {'the source payload'} after the no-op got {'what it holds'}\", Exit 95.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the payload assertion'.
    'gen emit' of "{indent}Print {'the possessive'} type.\n".

(VAL-14 (LANGUAGE.md:2769-2776): the `type` property reads the runtime
 tag and returns a text description with a `(dynamic)` suffix - `Text
 (dynamic)`, `Number (dynamic)`, `Float (dynamic)`, `Boolean (dynamic)`,
 `List (dynamic)`, `Map (dynamic)`, `Nothing (dynamic)`. The manual
 (LANGUAGE.md:2780) says those seven are the whole list, so a tag
 outside them is itself a finding.

 The generator declares the value, so it knows the tag, so it asserts
 the exact string rather than printing it. Which tags a given emission
 covers is NOT pinned by the row - the row asks for the property, not
 for a fixed roll call - so the count and the tags are drawn, and a
 campaign covers all seven many times over. Emitting the same seven in
 the same order every time would put a fixed vocabulary of seven lines
 into every program that draws this leaf, which is precisely the
 undeclared rule CLAUDE.md forbids.)

To 'gen leaf value type property' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    a number called 'how many tags' is 'rng below' of 6 add 2.
    a number called 'the rotation' is 'rng below' of 7.
    a number called 'the stride' is 'rng below' of 6 add 1.
    a number called 'tags shown' is 0.
    a text called 'the last possessive' is "".
    While 'tags shown' is less than 'how many tags',
        a number called 'the step' is 'tags shown' multiply 'the stride',
        a number called 'the slot' is 'the step' add 'the rotation',
        a number called 'the tag' is 'the slot' modulo 7,
        a text called 'the payload' is 'gen value payload' of 'the tag',
        a text called 'the literal' is 'gen value expression' of 'the tag' and 'the payload',
        a text called 'the phrase' is 'gen fresh noun',
        a text called 'the name' is 'gen written name' of 'the phrase',
        a text called 'the possessive' is 'gen possessive name' of 'the phrase',
        a text called 'the type text' is 'gen dynamic type text' of 'the tag',
        a text called 'the tag it reported' is 'gen type phrase' of 'the possessive',
        'gen emit' of "{indent}a value called {'the name'} is {'the literal'}.\n",
        a text called 'the type assertion' is "{indent}If {'the possessive'} type is not \"{'the type text'}\" then, Print \"ASSERT VAL-14: expected {'the type text'} got {'the tag it reported'}\", Exit 95.\n",
        'gen emit' of 'the type assertion',
        Set 'the last possessive' to 'the possessive',
        Set 'tags shown' to 'tags shown' add 1.
    'gen emit' of "{indent}Print {'the last possessive'} type.\n".

(VAL-21 (LANGUAGE.md:2827-2839): `nothing` is the absent value, and it
 can sit in a list slot, a map value, or a `value` local. All three
 positions in one leaf, each read back into a `value` local and asserted
 with `is nothing` - which LANGUAGE.md:2845 says is the test, there
 being no `is a nothing` predicate.

 A slot that is NOT the absent one is asserted too, in the opposite
 direction: a runtime that answered `is nothing` for everything would
 pass the first three assertions and fail this one.

 All three spellings are drawn ('gen value payload' of tag 6 does the
 drawing), because LANGUAGE.md:2841 says `nothing`, `null` and `nil`
 produce the identical value and picking one always would be a rule
 nobody wrote. Which slot of the list and which key of the map hold the
 absent value are drawn for the same reason.)

To 'gen leaf absent value' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    a text called 'the list phrase' is 'gen fresh noun'.
    a text called 'the list name' is 'gen written name' of 'the list phrase'.
    a number called 'how many slots' is 'rng below' of 4 add 2.
    a number called 'the absent slot' is 'rng below' of 'how many slots' add 1.
    a number called 'the filled slot' is 'rng below' of 'how many slots' add 1.
    While 'the filled slot' is equal to 'the absent slot',
        Set 'the filled slot' to 'rng below' of 'how many slots' add 1.
    a text called 'the slots' is "".
    a number called 'slots built' is 0.
    While 'slots built' is less than 'how many slots',
        a number called 'this slot' is 'slots built' add 1,
        a text called 'the element' is 'gen scalar element',
        If 'this slot' is equal to 'the absent slot' then,
            Set 'the element' to 'gen value payload' of 6.
        If 'slots built' is 0 then,
            Set 'the slots' to 'the element'.
        If 'slots built' is greater than 0 then,
            Set 'the slots' to "{'the slots'}, {'the element'}".
        Set 'slots built' to 'slots built' add 1.
    'gen emit' of "{indent}a list called {'the list name'} is [{'the slots'}].\n".
    a text called 'the empty slot phrase' is 'gen fresh noun'.
    a text called 'the empty slot name' is 'gen written name' of 'the empty slot phrase'.
    a text called 'the empty slot possessive' is 'gen possessive name' of 'the empty slot phrase'.
    a text called 'what the empty slot reported' is 'gen type phrase' of 'the empty slot possessive'.
    'gen emit' of "{indent}a value called {'the empty slot name'} is element {'the absent slot'} of {'the list name'}.\n".
    a text called 'the slot assertion' is "{indent}If {'the empty slot name'} is not nothing then, Print \"ASSERT VAL-21: expected nothing in slot {'the absent slot'} got {'what the empty slot reported'}\", Exit 95.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the slot assertion'.
    a text called 'the full slot phrase' is 'gen fresh noun'.
    a text called 'the full slot name' is 'gen written name' of 'the full slot phrase'.
    a text called 'the full slot possessive' is 'gen possessive name' of 'the full slot phrase'.
    a text called 'what the full slot reported' is 'gen type phrase' of 'the full slot possessive'.
    'gen emit' of "{indent}a value called {'the full slot name'} is element {'the filled slot'} of {'the list name'}.\n".
    a text called 'the filled slot assertion' is "{indent}If {'the full slot name'} is nothing then, Print \"ASSERT VAL-21: expected a value in slot {'the filled slot'} got {'what the full slot reported'}\", Exit 95.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the filled slot assertion'.
    (The map position. The absent key is drawn first and every other key
     is drawn to differ from it, so the entry read back is the entry
     written - a map literal with the key twice would answer with
     whichever entry won, and the assertion would be about the wrong
     one.)
    a text called 'the map phrase' is 'gen fresh noun'.
    a text called 'the map name' is 'gen written name' of 'the map phrase'.
    a text called 'the map possessive' is 'gen possessive name' of 'the map phrase'.
    a text called 'the absent key' is 'gen word from' of 'the value nouns'.
    a number called 'how many entries' is 'rng below' of 3 add 1.
    a number called 'the absent entry' is 'rng below' of 'how many entries' add 1.
    a text called 'the entries' is "".
    a number called 'entries built' is 0.
    While 'entries built' is less than 'how many entries',
        a number called 'this entry' is 'entries built' add 1,
        a text called 'the key' is 'gen noun other than' of 'the absent key',
        a text called 'the mapped value' is 'gen scalar element',
        If 'this entry' is equal to 'the absent entry' then,
            Set 'the key' to 'the absent key',
            Set 'the mapped value' to 'gen value payload' of 6.
        a text called 'the entry' is "\"{'the key'}\": {'the mapped value'}",
        If 'entries built' is 0 then,
            Set 'the entries' to 'the entry'.
        If 'entries built' is greater than 0 then,
            Set 'the entries' to "{'the entries'}, {'the entry'}".
        Set 'entries built' to 'entries built' add 1.
    'gen emit' of "{indent}a map called {'the map name'} is {{{'the entries'}}}.\n".
    a text called 'the entry phrase' is 'gen fresh noun'.
    a text called 'the entry name' is 'gen written name' of 'the entry phrase'.
    a text called 'the entry possessive' is 'gen possessive name' of 'the entry phrase'.
    a text called 'what the entry reported' is 'gen type phrase' of 'the entry possessive'.
    'gen emit' of "{indent}a value called {'the entry name'} is {'the map possessive'} \"{'the absent key'}\".\n".
    a text called 'the entry assertion' is "{indent}If {'the entry name'} is not nothing then, Print \"ASSERT VAL-21: expected nothing at {'the absent key'} got {'what the entry reported'}\", Exit 95.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the entry assertion'.
    (The `value` local position - the absent value written straight into
     a declaration rather than read out of an aggregate.)
    a text called 'the local phrase' is 'gen fresh noun'.
    a text called 'the local name' is 'gen written name' of 'the local phrase'.
    a text called 'the local possessive' is 'gen possessive name' of 'the local phrase'.
    a text called 'what the local reported' is 'gen type phrase' of 'the local possessive'.
    a text called 'the absent spelling' is 'gen value payload' of 6.
    'gen emit' of "{indent}a value called {'the local name'} is {'the absent spelling'}.\n".
    a text called 'the local assertion' is "{indent}If {'the local name'} is not nothing then, Print \"ASSERT VAL-21: expected nothing got {'what the local reported'}\", Exit 95.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the local assertion'.
    a text called 'the local type assertion' is "{indent}If {'the local possessive'} type is not \"Nothing (dynamic)\" then, Print \"ASSERT VAL-21: expected Nothing (dynamic) got {'what the local reported'}\", Exit 95.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the local type assertion'.
    'gen emit' of "{indent}Print {'the list name'}.\n".

(VAL-25 (LANGUAGE.md:2845-2851): `is nothing` and `is not nothing` are
 the test, and they are an EQUALITY like `is true`, not a type
 predicate - there is no `is a nothing`.

 Both spellings are asserted in both directions, on an absent value and
 on a present one, which is four assertions and needs all four: a
 runtime that answered `is nothing` for everything would pass two of
 them, and one that answered it for nothing would pass the other two.

 The two directions that must be TRUE are asserted through a witness
 rather than an `Otherwise` branch, so every line closes the clause it
 opens - an assertion that ended on `Otherwise, ...` would leave the
 else branch continuing into whatever the generator emitted next
 (gen_buffers.vox's 'gen assert number' has the full account).)

To 'gen leaf absent test' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    a text called 'the absent phrase' is 'gen fresh noun'.
    a text called 'the absent name' is 'gen written name' of 'the absent phrase'.
    a text called 'the absent possessive' is 'gen possessive name' of 'the absent phrase'.
    a text called 'what the absent one reported' is 'gen type phrase' of 'the absent possessive'.
    a text called 'the absent spelling' is 'gen value payload' of 6.
    a number called 'the present tag' is 'rng below' of 6.
    a text called 'the present payload' is 'gen value payload' of 'the present tag'.
    a text called 'the present literal' is 'gen value expression' of 'the present tag' and 'the present payload'.
    a text called 'the present phrase' is 'gen fresh noun'.
    a text called 'the present name' is 'gen written name' of 'the present phrase'.
    a text called 'the present possessive' is 'gen possessive name' of 'the present phrase'.
    a text called 'what the present one reported' is 'gen type phrase' of 'the present possessive'.
    a text called 'the absent witness phrase' is 'gen fresh noun'.
    a text called 'the absent witness name' is 'gen written name' of 'the absent witness phrase'.
    a text called 'the present witness phrase' is 'gen fresh noun'.
    a text called 'the present witness name' is 'gen written name' of 'the present witness phrase'.
    'gen emit' of "{indent}a value called {'the absent name'} is {'the absent spelling'}.\n".
    'gen emit' of "{indent}a value called {'the present name'} is {'the present literal'}.\n".
    'gen emit' of "{indent}a boolean called {'the absent witness name'} is false.\n".
    'gen emit' of "{indent}If {'the absent name'} is nothing then, Set {'the absent witness name'} to true.\n".
    a text called 'the absent holds' is "{indent}If {'the absent witness name'} is false then, Print \"ASSERT VAL-25: expected is nothing to hold got {'what the absent one reported'}\", Exit 95.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the absent holds'.
    a text called 'the absent denial' is "{indent}If {'the absent name'} is not nothing then, Print \"ASSERT VAL-25: expected is not nothing to be false got {'what the absent one reported'}\", Exit 95.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the absent denial'.
    'gen emit' of "{indent}a boolean called {'the present witness name'} is false.\n".
    'gen emit' of "{indent}If {'the present name'} is not nothing then, Set {'the present witness name'} to true.\n".
    a text called 'the present holds' is "{indent}If {'the present witness name'} is false then, Print \"ASSERT VAL-25: expected is not nothing to hold got {'what the present one reported'}\", Exit 95.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the present holds'.
    a text called 'the present denial' is "{indent}If {'the present name'} is nothing then, Print \"ASSERT VAL-25: expected is nothing to be false got {'what the present one reported'}\", Exit 95.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the present denial'.
    'gen emit' of "{indent}Print {'the absent witness name'}.\n".

(VAL-27 (LANGUAGE.md:2863-2872): reading a map key that was never set is
 an ERROR, not `nothing` - the read raises the error flag rather than
 silently handing back an absent value, so "the key is absent" and "the
 key holds nothing" stay distinguishable.

 What this leaf must NOT do is assert the missing read equals `nothing`:
 that it does not is the entire claim. The assertion is on the flag, via
 `On error`, and the contrast entry - a key that IS present and holds
 `nothing` - is asserted the other way: it reads back as nothing and
 raises no flag at all.

 Both handlers sit behind a drained one, so a flag left standing by an
 earlier leaf cannot make the absent read look caught, nor the present
 read look guilty.

 The absent key comes from 'the absent keys', a vocabulary kept disjoint
 from the one the present keys are drawn from - the row's claim is only
 tested if the key really is missing, and a key drawn from the same
 words could land on one that was written.)

To 'gen leaf absent key' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    a text called 'the map phrase' is 'gen fresh noun'.
    a text called 'the map name' is 'gen written name' of 'the map phrase'.
    a text called 'the map possessive' is 'gen possessive name' of 'the map phrase'.
    a text called 'the present key' is 'gen word from' of 'the value nouns'.
    a text called 'the missing key' is 'gen word from' of 'the absent keys'.
    (How many entries stand beside the one that holds nothing. Zero is
     reachable and legal - a map whose only entry is the absent value -
     and nothing says a map must be bigger than that.)
    a number called 'how many extra entries' is 'rng below' of 3.
    a text called 'the absent spelling' is 'gen value payload' of 6.
    a text called 'the entries' is "\"{'the present key'}\": {'the absent spelling'}".
    a number called 'entries built' is 0.
    While 'entries built' is less than 'how many extra entries',
        a text called 'another key' is 'gen noun other than' of 'the present key',
        a text called 'another value' is 'gen scalar element',
        Set 'the entries' to "{'the entries'}, \"{'another key'}\": {'another value'}",
        Set 'entries built' to 'entries built' add 1.
    'gen emit' of "{indent}a map called {'the map name'} is {{{'the entries'}}}.\n".
    (The receiving type of the missing read is drawn: the manual's own
     example reads into a `number`, but the error is the READ's, not the
     receiver's, and nothing pins which type is asked to take it.

     `a text` is NOT among them, and this is the one place a rule really
     does pin the shape. The compiler resolves a never-set key at COMPILE
     time - it knows the literal key is not in the literal map - and
     rejects `a text called <x> is <map>'s "<missing>"` outright, saying
     the read yields the number 0. So a text receiver is a known compile
     error, and the generator's contract is legal Vox that should compile
     AND run (CLAUDE.md); emitting one would be a generator defect, not a
     finding. The compile-time half of this behaviour is undocumented -
     LANGUAGE.md:2863 describes the missing read as a runtime error only -
     and is in the batch report as a candidate for the master.)
    a number called 'the receiver choice' is 'rng below' of 2.
    a text called 'the receiver type' is "a number".
    If 'the receiver choice' is 1 then,
        Set 'the receiver type' to "a value".
    a text called 'the reading phrase' is 'gen fresh noun'.
    a text called 'the reading name' is 'gen written name' of 'the reading phrase'.
    a text called 'the witness phrase' is 'gen fresh noun'.
    a text called 'the witness name' is 'gen written name' of 'the witness phrase'.
    'gen emit' of "{indent}a number called {'the witness name'} is 0.\n".
    'gen drain the error flag' of indent and 'the witness name'.
    'gen emit' of "{indent}{'the receiver type'} called {'the reading name'} is {'the map possessive'} \"{'the missing key'}\".\n".
    'gen emit' of "{indent}On error Set {'the witness name'} to 1.\n".
    a text called 'the flag assertion' is "{indent}If {'the witness name'} is not 1 then, Print \"ASSERT VAL-27: expected reading the never-set key {'the missing key'} to raise the error flag got {{{'the witness name'}}}\", Exit 95.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the flag assertion'.
    (The contrast: the key that IS there and holds nothing reads back as
     nothing, quietly.)
    a text called 'the entry phrase' is 'gen fresh noun'.
    a text called 'the entry name' is 'gen written name' of 'the entry phrase'.
    a text called 'the entry possessive' is 'gen possessive name' of 'the entry phrase'.
    a text called 'what the entry reported' is 'gen type phrase' of 'the entry possessive'.
    a text called 'the second witness phrase' is 'gen fresh noun'.
    a text called 'the second witness name' is 'gen written name' of 'the second witness phrase'.
    'gen emit' of "{indent}a number called {'the second witness name'} is 0.\n".
    'gen drain the error flag' of indent and 'the second witness name'.
    'gen emit' of "{indent}a value called {'the entry name'} is {'the map possessive'} \"{'the present key'}\".\n".
    'gen emit' of "{indent}On error Set {'the second witness name'} to 1.\n".
    a text called 'the quiet assertion' is "{indent}If {'the second witness name'} is not 0 then, Print \"ASSERT VAL-27: expected reading the present key {'the present key'} to raise no flag got {{{'the second witness name'}}}\", Exit 95.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the quiet assertion'.
    a text called 'the present assertion' is "{indent}If {'the entry name'} is not nothing then, Print \"ASSERT VAL-27: expected nothing at the present key {'the present key'} got {'what the entry reported'}\", Exit 95.\n".
    'gen emit' of 'the present assertion'.
    'gen emit' of "{indent}Print {'the witness name'}.\n".
